)^{2}=4$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433818 1072 #uuid "3df7ca0c-a7bc-5b5f-9b3f-4b5360131dc4" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433818 1074 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(0-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+9 & =4 \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x-2)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x-2)^{2}=-5.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/4b/4b56ce205a771f9683aefb65f1953aab927cf3388f7f9375a6146dc4300a67a9.png)" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433813 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1069 "q-54224" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1071 "![](images/79/793009824d6d5a75f934fa3cfb60dd7e1b05b2918c6fef605777221bae3898af.png)\n\nFind the $y$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y=-5,$ shown above." 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1072 #uuid "727fd4af-87ee-5f68-9fac-4f3bb9ee42b6" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433819 1074 "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4x-6y & =-5 \\\\ (0)^{2}+{y}^{2}+4(0)-6y & =-5 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-6y+9 & =-5+9 \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-3 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =3\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,1)$ and $(0,5).$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433817 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1069 "q-160269" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1071 "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=2$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1072 #uuid "85a89c6d-abe9-53d6-8315-1fd338cd6cd0" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433820 1074 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+(0+2)^{2} & =2 \\\\ (x+2)^{2}+4 & =2 \\\\ (x+2)^{2} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x+2)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x+2)^{2}=-2.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e5/e57f57f3e0cff36d9cc89a8889fa2f7fa5f4e8f9ceb5703c2d16f4ea16f38174.png)" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433816 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1069 "q-7536" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1071 "![](images/29/299ca5fbab1351ab47dc2be6adac47b3ba3daf747e54c9b41042076cd2fee669.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5,$ shown above." 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1072 #uuid "9985268c-7921-5895-ae59-048de6962883" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433821 1074 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(\\sqrt{5},0).$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433814 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1069 "q-7542" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1071 "![](images/93/938eab916bca20cff978e937cbcdf02391ce9c840b996dae969fd3b616b83294.png)\n\nFind the $y$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10.$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1072 #uuid "ce9524f3-b3f6-5df0-a247-5d8e5bf9f0d4" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433822 1074 "We must have $x=0$ at the $y$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ {0}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =10 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y$-intercepts occur at the points $(0,-\\sqrt{10})$ and $(0,\\sqrt{10}).$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433815 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1069 "q-7555" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1071 "![](images/53/533a1d7aaa5cc94ed737e665189d3722582e83c3b556bce13ec0d4d0c547ffc8.png)\n\nFind the $x$-intercepts of the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=9,$ shown above." 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1072 #uuid "f69cf1ca-47a0-5c1a-89a4-ba27600434f1" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true] [17592186433823 1074 "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts. \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(0+2)^{2} & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+4 & =9 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =5 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{5} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts occur at the points $(1-\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(1+\\sqrt{5},0).$" 13194139534718 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0d31dc8e-0c35-5fd0-abcd-c7628cdd0a04" 17592186433782 "answ